// E0507 — A `Drop::drop` BODY MAY NOT MOVE A FIELD OF `self` OUT.
// ⚠ RENAMED FROM `_e0509` 2026-09-10 WITH THE STDLIB-`Drop` CORPUS CONVERSION,
//   AND THE NEW CODE IS THE RUST-CANONICAL ONE. The subject is unchanged. This
//   file used to declare its own by-value `trait Drop { fn drop(self: Self); }`;
//   it now binds the stdlib lang item, whose receiver is `&mut Self`, so the move
//   is refused for the REFERENCE and never reaches the E0509 arm. That is exactly
//   what rustc does: tests/ui/borrowck/borrowck-describe-field-generic-param-owned-box
//   moves `self.0` inside a `fn drop(&mut self)` body and its `.stderr` reads
//   `error[E0507]: cannot move out of `self.0` which is behind a mutable reference`.
//   E0509 is NOT lost: its Rust-canonical carrier is the move-out-of-a-Drop-type
//   pattern binding (upstream disallowed-deconstructing-destructing-struct-match),
//   and TEN fixtures in this tree still pin that sentence.
// the point. `@rule intrinsic.drop.move-out-of-drop-type-refused`.
//
// FAIL half of a pair. The pass half,
// tests/logos/pass/drop_body_conditional_move_e0507_ok, is the SAME program
// with the move statement DELETED (`if self.armed { }`), and it runs.
//
// Was soundness_queue row `drop_body_conditional_move_double_drops_both_paths`
// (tier 1, run 1), closed 2026-09-08. Before: the field was destroyed twice on
// BOTH paths — including the disarmed one, where the move never executes —
// because the caller's field recursion has no record of what the body consumed,
// and the drop flag that would carry it does not cross the call boundary. That
// is why no static skip could have been the answer: on the disarmed path a
// static skip turns the double free into a LEAK. The canonical rule removes the
// question by refusing the program.
//
// ⚠ THIS IS THE STDLIB'S OWN SHAPE. `stdlib/mem/manually_drop`'s `DropGuard`
// was written exactly like this, and was repaired the same day with Rust's
// escape hatch (`ManuallyDrop<F>` + `ptr::read`) — see
// tests/logos/pass/drop_guard_instantiated.
package drop_body_conditional_move_e0507;
extern fn malloc(n: i64) -> *mut u8;

struct N { w: i64, c: *mut i64 }
impl Drop for N { fn drop(self: &mut Self) { unsafe { self.c[0] = self.c[0] + self.w; } } }

struct G { armed: bool, f: N }
impl Drop for G { fn drop(self: &mut Self) { if self.armed { let q: N = self.f; } } }

unsafe fn main() -> i32 {
    let c: *mut i64 = malloc(8) as *mut i64;
    c[0] = 0i64;
    { let g: G = G { armed: false, f: N { w: 7i64, c: c } }; }
    if c[0] != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
